"""25 real user feedback responses (operator-provided, 2026-07-21) for the Cube 6
theming workflow test. Deduped from the pasted set (the Response-11/12 blocks
repeated). Each entry is a faithful excerpt capturing the persona's like +
dislike + improvement signal — enough for Theme 01 (Risk/Supporting/Neutral)
classification and Theme 02 (9/6/3) generation. Used by harness_cube6 +
test_harness_cube6 to run the REAL phase_b engine offline (no billed API).
"""

LIVE_FEEDBACK_25: list[dict] = [
    {"persona": "Innovation Project Manager", "text": "I have relied on this polling tool for over a year to collect and prioritize ideas. What I like most is the AI clustering of responses into themes combined with drag-and-rank; consensus in under 25 minutes. Pain points: live results lag 20-40 seconds with 180 participants, the mobile drag-and-drop barely works, customization and branding are minimal, and analytics stop at basic counts with no trend tracking or sentiment scoring."},
    {"persona": "High School Teacher", "text": "I use the polling tool almost daily for exit tickets and quick checks. I like the zero-friction entry, anonymous mode, and AI clustering that shows the common misconceptions instantly. What frustrates me is the lack of Google Classroom or Canvas integration, too many buttons for middle-schoolers, results that lag on old Chromebooks, and no graded-quiz or clean export for parent conferences."},
    {"persona": "Large Event Organizer", "text": "I run hybrid conferences for 300-1200 attendees. Real-time results and drag-rank for live Q&A have been game-changers and AI clustering cut post-mortem time in half. At 800+ users we see 15-30 second delays, there are almost no moderation controls, mobile support is inconsistent, branding is too basic for sponsors, and post-event reporting is rudimentary."},
    {"persona": "Data Analyst / BI Specialist", "text": "I turn feedback into dashboards. I appreciate clean CSV/JSON export and AI clustering as a first thematic pass. What I dislike is the lack of a proper API or webhooks, limited visualization options, no versioning of poll questions, and large exports that timeout or truncate. I want a documented REST and GraphQL API, advanced visualizations, and audit logging."},
    {"persona": "HR / Employee Engagement Lead", "text": "We run quarterly engagement surveys. I like the strong anonymity controls, the System of Innovation framing, and token rewards that raised response rates. I dislike the lack of enterprise compliance, no GDPR/CCPA proof or data-retention management, crude demographic slicing risking re-identification, no SSO or SCIM, and inconsistent mobile experience."},
    {"persona": "Software Developer / Power User", "text": "The real-time collaboration and AI assistance feel technically elegant. What frustrates me is the lack of a public API and webhooks, forcing brittle screen-scraping, sparse documentation, no sandbox environment, and missing versioning of poll definitions. I want a well-documented versioned REST/GraphQL API with OAuth2, webhooks for lifecycle events, and a developer portal."},
    {"persona": "Small Business Owner / Solopreneur", "text": "As the owner of a 12-person creative agency I need simple affordable tools. I like that it is easy to set up and the AI clustering helps make sense of client feedback without an analyst. Some features feel half-finished: the mobile view is clunky, there is no simple embed, reporting is basic with no one-page PDF, and support is slow during live workshops."},
    {"persona": "Accessibility & Inclusion Advocate", "text": "I evaluate tools for accessibility compliance. I like that basic keyboard navigation works and the anonymous option supports psychological safety. It falls short of WCAG 2.2 AA: inconsistent screen-reader support, focus management breaks on updates, no voice-input for open text, drag-and-drop has no accessible alternative, color is the only status indicator, and mobile touch targets are too small."},
    {"persona": "Frequent User Comparing to Competitors", "text": "I have used Mentimeter, Slido, and Google Forms and this tool sits in an interesting middle ground. I like the AI clustering, drag-rank, ethical framing, and the token system. It is missing battle-tested features: no live word-cloud or reactions, rudimentary quiz and scoring modes, no agenda or timer integration, a less mature analytics dashboard, and mobile parity behind competitors."},
    {"persona": "Long-term Visionary User", "text": "I appreciate the consistent focus on combining AI assistance with human authority and ethics, a true System of Innovation. What I dislike is that exciting capabilities feel half-baked behind technical debt: the AI sometimes produces generic clusters needing cleanup, the knowledge-graph features are promised but underdelivering, and mobile and accessibility gaps make it feel less universal than its ambitions."},
    {"persona": "University Professor / Academic Researcher", "text": "I use the tool in large lectures and seminars. I like the AI clustering of open-ended responses, transparent drag-and-rank, and anonymous contribution on sensitive issues. I dislike the limited ability to link results to learning outcomes, basic export forcing extra cleaning, no Canvas or Moodle integration, and an uneven mobile experience for students responding on phones."},
    {"persona": "Non-profit / Community Organizer", "text": "I coordinate community forums and participatory budgeting. I like the low barrier to entry and the visual ranking that lets residents prioritize fairly, plus AI clustering of free-text concerns. Frustrations are accessibility and trust: the mobile experience is too heavy on older phones and low data, no simple multi-language support, and unclear plain-language privacy explanations or data-deletion options."},
    {"persona": "Marketing & Brand Manager", "text": "I use it for rapid customer and stakeholder feedback on messaging and concepts. I like the fast setup and clean visual ranking that helps teams converge in one meeting, plus AI clustering that reveals language patterns. I dislike the limited branding control, weak export and presentation options requiring manual slide work, and no easy segmentation by customer segment or campaign wave."},
    {"persona": "Healthcare Administrator", "text": "In a hospital system we use it for staff feedback on workflow and quality projects. I like quick collection from busy clinicians, ranking that surfaces urgent problems, AI clustering catching issues incident systems miss, and essential anonymity. I dislike limited control over data retention and role-based access in a regulated environment, inconsistent mobile in low-connectivity areas, and reporting too basic for compliance committees."},
    {"persona": "Government / Public Sector Manager", "text": "I work in municipal government using it for process improvement and public consultation. I like the transparency of the ranking process, easy setup, and AI clustering that identifies recurring service issues. I dislike the lack of compliance and records-management features, insufficient documentation of data residency and retention, incomplete accessibility conformance, and no official timestamped reports for the public record."},
    {"persona": "Startup Founder", "text": "I use it internally and with early customers and advisors. I like the speed and low friction, spinning up a poll in minutes for directional signal, effective backlog prioritization, and AI clustering that reveals customer pain points. I dislike the limited ability to close the loop with participants, awkward mobile ranking, and shallow analytics once we have more than a few polls."},
    {"persona": "Freelance Consultant", "text": "I gather stakeholder input during strategy and change projects. I like the professional approachable interface, clear visual ranking that helps diverse stakeholders converge, and AI clustering I can bring into workshops the same day. I dislike the limited ability to brand per client, cumbersome switching between client contexts, export needing extra polish, and frequent mobile usability complaints."},
    {"persona": "University Student", "text": "I use it in classes and student organization meetings. I like that it is easy to join, the ranking feels interactive, live results make discussions dynamic, and anonymous contribution is appreciated. I dislike the cluttered interface on a phone, awkward ranking on small screens, little feedback after a poll closes about decisions made, and occasional lag during larger class sessions."},
    {"persona": "Product Manager", "text": "I use it for prioritization workshops, feature validation, and alignment across product, design, and engineering. I like the combination of qualitative clustering and quantitative ranking in one lightweight flow and the ethical framing around human decision rights. I dislike the lack of native integration with Jira or Linear, weak longitudinal tracking of shifting priorities, unreliable mobile ranking, and reporting that is not presentation-ready."},
    {"persona": "Customer Support Team Lead", "text": "Our support team uses it for internal process feedback and customer pulse checks. I like the speed of setup, clear ranking of painful issues, and AI clustering that identifies recurring friction points tickets do not surface. I dislike limited segmentation by team or shift, inconsistent mobile usability for agents on the move, and no easy way to link outcomes back to tickets or articles."},
    {"persona": "Remote / Distributed Team Lead", "text": "I manage a fully distributed team across time zones and use it for asynchronous prioritization. I like that people contribute on their own schedule and still see a clear ranked outcome, plus AI clustering when people cannot attend live. I dislike that the experience is optimized for synchronous use, limited async discussion on ranked items, basic notification and reminder options, and less fluid mobile ranking."},
    {"persona": "DEI Specialist", "text": "I gather input on inclusion initiatives and belonging surveys. I like the strong anonymity options, visual ranking that surfaces urgent issues for different groups, AI clustering revealing concerns formal surveys miss, and the ethical framing. I dislike the limited ability to analyze small vulnerable groups safely, demographic slicing that risks re-identification, insufficient safeguards for sensitive feedback, and incomplete accessibility."},
    {"persona": "Financial Analyst / Planning Team", "text": "We use it for internal prioritization of budget initiatives and planning exercises. I like the clear ranking of options, fast cycle time, and AI clustering of supporting comments that adds qualitative context. I dislike the limited ability to attach structured cost, impact, or risk data to ranked items, export requiring manual transcription into models, and little support for scenario comparison."},
    {"persona": "Legal / Compliance Officer", "text": "I evaluate tools for regulated environments. I like the relative transparency of the ranking process, basic audit information, and appropriate anonymity options. I dislike the incomplete controls around data retention, access logging, and records management, insufficient documentation of data flows and processing activities, accessibility gaps, and limited ability to produce complete defensible records of a consultation or decision process."},
    {"persona": "Creative Agency / Design Team Lead", "text": "Our agency uses it for creative prioritization and client concept selection. I like the visual interactive ranking that feels natural for creative teams and AI clustering that surfaces emotional responses influencing direction. I dislike the limited visual and branding control, export needing extra design work for client presentations, less fluid mobile ranking, and no ability to attach reference images to ranked options."},
]
